# Backgammon on the C64 (c64/draw/backgammon.c): a checker (16 by 16, two cells by two: a solid disc 14
# across, drawn as a circle, with a pixel of its place's color round it, so that stacked checkers have a line of it between
# them), the counts cut out of a stack's last checker (16 by 8, drawn exclusive-or over the disc's middle
# rows: the digits 2 to 9 and +, 6 by 8 in columns 5 to 10), the points' tips (16 by 8, pointing down for
# the top row and up for the bottom one), the dice (8 by 8, black pips on white) and the gliding checker,
# a sprite of the same disc. Made for this program.

